# https://w3id.org/laderr#disabled
<https://w3id.org/laderr#disabled> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/laderr#disabled> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/laderr#DispositionState> .
<https://w3id.org/laderr#disabled> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Represents a DispositionState where a Capability or Vulnerability is inactive and cannot influence the system. A disabled Disposition cannot exert its effect until it is re-enabled."@en .
<https://w3id.org/laderr#disabled> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/laderr> .
<https://w3id.org/laderr#disabled> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "disabled"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/laderr#enabled
<https://w3id.org/laderr#enabled> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/laderr#enabled> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/laderr#DispositionState> .
<https://w3id.org/laderr#enabled> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Represents a DispositionState where a Capability or Vulnerability is active and can influence the system. An enabled Capability can, e.g., sustain a resilience, while an enabled Vulnerability can be exploited by threats."@en .
<https://w3id.org/laderr#enabled> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/laderr> .
<https://w3id.org/laderr#enabled> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "enabled"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/laderr#incident
